What are Inspection Robots?
Inspection Robots are autonomous or remote-operated systems equipped with cameras, sensors, and AI technologies designed for examining infrastructure in hazardous or inaccessible environments. These robots enable precise visual inspections, ultrasonic testing, and thermal imaging across critical processes such as pipeline monitoring, tank integrity checks, and structural assessments. Common types include crawler-based robots, unmanned aerial vehicles (UAVs), wheeled platforms, and articulated arm systems.
